Chapter 38: The Outer Edge
The heavy military transport transport hovered thirty feet above the desolate, ash-covered treeline of Sector 10’s northern perimeter. Beyond the high perimeter wall lay the Outer Frontier—a lawless, unmonitored expanse of dense pine forests, jagged rock canyons, and unstable rift zones.
PNEUMATIC HISS!
The transport's rear cargo ramp lowered into the damp morning air, revealing a jagged, glowing purple tear suspended in the atmosphere three hundred meters ahead: Class-B Outpost Rift #42.
Standing on the tarmac below were two squads assigned to the joint clearance operation.
On the left stood Ironclad Squad 2, led by Senior Vanguard Officer Marcus—a veteran Tier-B Hunter wearing heavy, polished kinetic power-armor, flanked by three senior corporate operatives carrying high-frequency alloy broadswords and tactical rifles.
On the right stood Anvil Ridge Squad 4. Renna stood at the front in her clean Vanguard Reserve uniform, her tower shield gleaming, with Tobias and Mina braced behind her. Three paces to her rear sat Kaelen, slouched on a wooden supply crate, holding a heavy leather repair kit and a pair of scrap tongs, wearing his loose utility vest over his uniform.
Underneath his loose vest, Kaelen's newly forged [Hydra's Void-Scale Harness] rested invisibly against his chest, humming with cold, suppressed power alongside his 101 Strength and 102 Agility.
Senior Officer Marcus stepped forward, his heavy steel boots crunching on the gravel as he looked down at Squad 4 with open disdain.
"So this is the auxiliary reserve unit Vanguard assigned to my perimeter sweep," Marcus sneered, his cold eyes flicking over Renna's shield before landing on Kaelen holding his oil rag. "Listen closely, freshmen. Out here in the Frontier, there are no arena barriers, no emergency stop switches, and no medical teams waiting around the corner."
Marcus tapped his gauntlet console, displaying a holographic map of the rift zone.
"Outpost Rift #42 is a high-density woodland environment populated by Iron-Claw Stalkers (Tier-C) and Grave-Vine Abominations (Tier-C Elite)," Marcus instructed flatly. "My squad will take the primary central path and secure the Rift Core. You three reserves will hold the western drainage flank and clear low-tier stragglers."
He then glanced at Kaelen, letting out a dry scoff. "And make sure your caddy stays ten meters behind the shield line. If he panics and steps into a vine trap, we aren't stopping the sweep to haul his corpse out."
"My team knows how to secure a flank, Senior Officer," Renna replied coldly, her amber eyes locking onto Marcus without flinching.
"We'll see," Marcus grunted, turning back to his men. "Ironclad, move out!"
Five minutes later, Squad 4 stepped through the pulsing, atmospheric barrier of Outpost Rift #42.
The interior of the rift was a dark, twisting forest of towering obsidian trees and thick, purple-tinged fog that dampened sound. The ground was slick with black mud and rotting vegetation.
Renna led the formation along the muddy western drainage ravine, her tower shield raised, while Tobias scanned the high branches with his loaded crossbow and Mina held her dual daggers low.
Kaelen slouched behind Renna’s left heel, dragging an iron salvage crate through the mud and putting on a breathless, nervous facade.
BZZZZT.
Behind his lowered hood, Kaelen engaged [Phantom Kinetic Cloak].
The active utility skill activated instantly, erasing his outward mana signature, heat profile, and heartbeat from the surrounding environment. To any detection sensor, thermal scanner, or monster in the forest, Kaelen Vance was completely invisible—nothing more than ambient air.
Simultaneously, his passive [Hive-Mind Synapse] and [Low-Light Spatial Perception] flared to life, mapping the entire five-kilometer forest grid in crystal-clear detail.
Ironclad Squad 2 has already broken formation, Kaelen calculated silently, tracking the energy signatures through the trees. They aren't heading for the Rift Core. Marcus is purposefully pulling the central monster nest toward our western flank.
Kaelen's eyes narrowed.
It wasn't a standard sweep. Senior Officer Marcus and Ironclad were deliberately sabotaging Squad 4's sector—funneling a horde of Tier-C Elite beasts straight toward Renna's position to trigger a barrier failure, ruin their 90-day reserve audit, and claim sole ownership of the Class-B Rift rewards.
Ahead in the thick fog, the high branches rustled violently.
Red, glowing eyes ignited in the canopy as twelve Iron-Claw Stalkers (Tier-C) and two massive, ten-foot Grave-Vine Abominations (Tier-C Elite) began slithering down the trunk walls, closing off the ravine's exit.
"CONTACT!" Tobias yelled, his voice cracking as he aimed his crossbow into the mist. "THERE ARE TOO MANY! THEY'RE FLANKING US FROM THE TREES!"
Renna slammed her tower shield into the mud, her jaw set with fierce determination. "HOLD THE CHOKE-POINT! TOBIAS, COVER THE HIGH BRANCHES! MINA, WATCH THE LEFT!"
Sitting behind Renna's heels in the fog, Kaelen slowly set his scrap tongs down on the iron crate.
His weak, timid expression faded into a cold, lethal calm.
"Renna," Kaelen stammered softly, stepping backward into the thick purple fog behind a massive obsidian tree. "I... I'll check the rear pipe to make sure nothing sneaks up from behind us!"
"Stay hidden, Kaelen!" Renna shouted over the sound of her shield absorbing a heavy claws-strike. "Don't come out until I call you!"
"Got it," Kaelen whispered.
The second he stepped behind the trunk, completely out of sight of his team, Kaelen’s slouched posture vanished.
He activated [Lightning-Phase Blitz].
ZAP!
A blinding arc of silent electric-blue lightning coated his frame. Moving at his base 102 Agility, Kaelen blurred into the deep forest shadows—not away from the battle, but straight into the dark canopy above the sabotaging Ironclad squad.
It was time to clear the Frontier.
